camera page: window insets that settle, a window service, JPEG stills, external textures, and frame rates a UVC camera accepts

Instagram 455's camera page (story / post / reel capture, QuickCaptureFragment)
stayed black. Five independent gaps, found in order:

1. View.requestApplyInsets() only flagged the view it was called on; the driver
   dispatches insets from the root and reads the flag there. Now it climbs to the
   root and schedules a traversal, as requestFitSystemWindows does on AOSP.
2. ServiceManager.getService("window") returned null. Instagram's
   WindowInsetsManager reflects IWindowManager.hasNavigationBar() and casts that
   result to a non-null IBinder: an NPE out of its insets listener, so its bar
   sizes stayed -1 and the 35 tasks waiting on them (the camera page among them)
   never ran. An inert Binder for "window" lets it reach the reflection failure it
   already handles.
3. The camera advertised YUV_420_888 only; Optic sizes its still stream from the
   JPEG sizes first and failed with "Invalid picture size: 'null'". JPEG is now in
   the stream configuration map (it is mandatory on every camera2 device), and a
   single capture that targets a JPEG ImageReader gets that frame encoded at the
   reader's size and JPEG_QUALITY (ImageReader gains an encoded-image queue: one
   plane, strides 0).
4. Setting the frame rate of a UVC camera to a rate between its listed ones threw
   NSInvalidArgumentException inside a JNI call: SIGABRT (Logitech C922). The rate
   now uses the listed range's own durations; @try is the backstop.
5. ANGLE-Metal has no GL_OES_EGL_image_external; SurfaceTexture already uploads
   each camera frame as GL_TEXTURE_2D. The GLES bridge now compiles a
   samplerExternalOES shader as sampler2D and routes GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES
   binds / parameters to GL_TEXTURE_2D (MACAPK_GL_EXTERNAL_AS_2D=0 turns it off).
   The INVALID_ENUM those binds raised was read by the frame upload as its own
   error ("first camera-frame GL upload reported error 0x500").

Also: MediaStore.Images/Video.Thumbnails.getThumbnail through loadThumbnail (AOSP
29+), loadThumbnail logs its first failures, onViewAttachedToWindow throws go to
GfxTrace.swallow, and MACAPK_DUMP_FRAGMENTS prints the fragment tree with each
fragment's state on the harness dump cadence.

Measured on Instagram 455 with a Logitech C922: the camera page lays out, the
preview is live and upright in story and post modes, a photo shared to the story
target opens the story editor. Open: the shutter does not react to a tap, and the
gallery grid on that page keeps empty cells (its thumbnail loader never asks).

